<article class="env-remark" id="04M7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04M7">Remark <span data-tag="04M7">78.20.4</span>.</a> In future chapters we will use the ambiguous notation where instead of writing $\mathcal{S}_ X$ for the stack in sets associated to $X$ we simply write $X$. Using this notation the diagram of Lemma <a href="/tag/044S" data-tag="044S">78.20.3</a> becomes the familiar diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ R \ar[r]_ s \ar[d]_ t &  U \ar[d]^\pi \\  U \ar[r]^-\pi &  [U/R] }  \]
</div>
  <p> In the following sections we will show that this diagram has many good properties. In particular we will show that it is a $2$-fibre product (Section <a href="/tag/04M8" data-tag="04M8">78.22</a>) and that it is close to being a $2$-coequalizer of $s$ and $t$ (Section <a href="/tag/04MA" data-tag="04MA">78.23</a>). </p>
</article>